Given the following file foo.js, which is tab indented:

``` js
function foo() {
    if (true) {
        console.log('foo');
    }
}
```

Running `eslint --no-eslintrc --fix --rule 'indent: "warn"' foo.js` changes foo.js to:

``` js
function foo() {
                                            if (true) {
                                                console.log('foo');
    }
}
```

This has inserted 40 spaces on lines 2 and 3. This isn't idempotent, running the same command again gives:

``` js
function foo() {
                                                                                    if (true) {
                                                                                        console.log('foo');
    }
}
```

I'm using v3.2.2 with the default parser.

I was expecting eslint to replace the tabs with spaces. Failing that, I would have expected eslint to choose a size of tab so it can calculate the indent consistently, so `--fix` is idempotent for this rule.
